  "interpretation": [
    "The fixed generated-only candidate did not meet its prespecified material-value criterion. Retain the result and the explicit production Drive DNA dimensions; this is not a field verdict on every embedding.",
    "Both methods retrieve 80/80 supported validation programs with macro F1/MRR 1.0 and detect 40/40 controlled changed pairs. The embedding flags 2/40 stable pairs versus 5/40 for normalized summaries, with no generated cohort regression.",
    "The lower stable-pair false-flag count is a synthetic signal, not validated real-drive FPR. The frozen gate requires retrieval-F1 or changed-detection improvement; neither improved. It was not broadened after observing the lower false-flag count.",
    "Both abstain before inference on all 24 missing/unsupported/stationary validation diagnostics. Scope/version checks bind actual weights/normalizer as well as external identity; no incompatible coordinate-space comparisons are permitted.",
    "Test structure/metadata was validated, but test predictions and metrics remain uncomputed after validation failure. No after-result model, noise, cutoff, baseline or gate tuning was performed.",
    "Shared generated programs and fictional scopes are not independent real-driver/style/vehicle evidence. These inputs are physical summaries, not accepted production dimensions or a feature adapter. Distances and cutoffs are not confidence, impairment, fatigue or safety judgments.",
    "Three latent coordinates versus eight summaries and the safe JSON checkpoint size do not establish mobile speed, battery or useful real-world compression. All earlier model and physical acceptance remains open."
  ],
